# What this corpus claims to describe.
#
# Git pathspecs, one per line, blank lines and # comments ignored. When a commit
# touches any of these and the corpus has not moved since, fixture-keeper is
# woken to decide whether any persona's expect block is now understated,
# overstated, or silent about a new behavior.
#
# This list lives with the corpus rather than in the watcher for two reasons.
# The corpus is the thing making the claim, so the claim's scope belongs next to
# it and moves when fixture-keeper changes what it covers. And the invariant in
# test/invariants.test.ts forbids anything under automation/ from naming the
# record's modules at all, bluntly and on purpose, which is the correct rule and
# not one to work around.
#
# Keep it narrow. A change to the HTTP surface or the CLI cannot make a claim
# about the mastery model false, and waking a lane for it teaches the lane to
# ignore its own watcher.

src/domain/
src/db/schema.sql
src/db/migrations/
src/record/
src/curriculum/
